# Proof-or-Stop (Always)

Agent output = **claim**. Lifecycle state (`done` / `fixed` / `shipped` / `tests pass`) admits only with **same-turn evidence**. No evidence → do not claim success.

**Also follow:** `aiimin-anti-lie.mdc` (truth labels, receipts, independent verification, discrepancy → guardrail).

## Statuses (only these)

| Status | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| `passed` | Required checks ran this turn and succeeded |
| `failed` | Checks ran; did not meet bar |
| `blocked` | Could not verify / ambiguous / need human — say why |
| `in progress` | Still working; no completion language |

Never: “done”, “fixed”, “all good”, “should work”, “LGTM” without evidence.

## Claim → required evidence (same turn)

| Claim | Must have this turn |
|-------|---------------------|
| Edited / added file | `Read` (or Grep) of that path showing the change |
| Bug fixed | Repro check or targeted test/command exit 0 + short result |
| Tests / build / lint pass | Command ran; exit 0 cited (no inventing) |
| Deployed / live / health OK | Real HTTP/health or deploy output this turn |
| “Not found” / “doesn’t exist” | Search/Grep/Glob ran; empty result cited |
| Vault / docs updated | Path named; change actually written |
| Commit / push / PR | Only after user ask + real git/`gh` result |

Skipped check ≠ pass. Missing tool result ≠ pass. **Fail closed** → `blocked` or `failed`.

## Closeout shape (when task ends)

1. What changed (paths only)
2. Evidence (command + exit, or confirming read/grep hit)
3. Status: `passed` | `failed` | `blocked`
4. If `blocked`/`failed`: next concrete step

No evidence block → cannot use completion language.

## Do not

- Grade own homework from memory of an earlier turn
- Say tests/deploy passed without running them this closeout
- Treat plan / intent / “I will” as done
- Hide uncertainty behind confident tone

## Token note

Keep evidence short: exit code + 1 decisive line, or 3–8 confirming source lines. No full log dumps unless user asks.
